One recommendation I'd make

Since QGuard Helix™ is evolving into a platform with multiple products, I would avoid making the subscriptions too tightly coupled.

Instead, think in terms of platform editions plus optional add-ons.

For example:

Starter – Messaging only
Basic – Messaging + Quantum Readiness
Professional – Adds Cloud Vault and limited Migration
Business – Full Migration + Cryptographic Asset Management
Enterprise – Everything plus enterprise integrations and support

Then allow organizations to purchase additional modules (for example, extra Cloud Vault storage, additional cryptographic asset capacity, advanced compliance packs, or professional services) without forcing them into a higher tier.

That gives customers flexibility while also creating clear upgrade paths as their needs grow. I think that approach aligns especially well with the long-term vision you've been building for QGuard Helix.